%N A400608 Integers q occurring in solutions of m^2 = p! * q! * r!, with p > q > r > 1, ordered by increasing m (A400208).
%C A400608 This sequence gives the corresponding values of q for the solutions to Problem 1, Round Two, of the 2023 New Zealand Mathematical Olympiad, which asks whether there exist infinitely many triples of integers p > q > r > 1 such that p! * q! * r! is a perfect square m^2.
%C A400608 Terms a(1) = 3!-1 and a(9) = 4!-1 come from the family (m, p, q, r) = ((t!)!, t!, t!-1, t), t >= 3. Here t = 3 and t = 4, respectively.
%C A400608 The family (p, q, r) = (k! * x^2, k! * x^2 - 1, k), k > 1, x >= 1, gives infinitely many solutions:
%C A400608 -> For r = 2, taking x = 2, 3, 4, 5 gives a(3) = 7, a(6) = 17, a(14) = 31, a(21) = 49.
%C A400608 -> For r = 3, taking x = 1, 2 gives a(1) = 5 and a(8) = 23.
%H A400608 New Zealand Mathematical Olympiad Committee, <a href="https://www.mathsolympiad.org.nz/competitions/nzmo/files/problems.php?round=2&amp;year=2023&amp;type=solutions">2023 NZMO Round 2, problem 1</a>.
%H A400608 <a href="/index/O#Olympiads">Index to sequences related to Olympiads and other Mathematical Competitions</a>.
%e A400608 For a(5) = 7, we have 10! * 7! * 6! = 3628800^2 = A400208(5)^2.
%Y A400608 Cf. A400208 (m), A400607 (p), this sequence (q), A400609 (r).
%K A400608 nonn
%O A400608 1,1
